1
00:00:00,191 --> 00:00:04,705
Deep in the sea, still
hidden, is the city of gold.

2
00:00:05,713 --> 00:00:10,218
And Shri Krishna, who built it,
could not save it from the waves.

3
00:00:11,315 --> 00:00:14,505
Just imagine, palaces,
markets and lanes,

4
00:00:14,525 --> 00:00:17,892
all gone beneath the
waves in a single day.

5
00:00:18,477 --> 00:00:20,469
This is Dwarka, Gujarat.

6
00:00:21,042 --> 00:00:24,961
Up here a temple flag
flutters, and down in the sea,

7
00:00:24,981 --> 00:00:27,406
an unsolved mystery lies hidden.

8
00:00:28,527 --> 00:00:31,896
So today we open up Dwarka
completely, its history,

9
00:00:31,916 --> 00:00:33,777
its mystery and the journey.

10
00:00:36,311 --> 00:00:41,013
Shri Krishna left Mathura, and built
a new capital by the western sea.

11
00:00:42,635 --> 00:00:46,047
He named it Dwarka,
which means a gateway.

12
00:00:46,531 --> 00:00:51,327
Years after the Mahabharata war,
the Yadava clan split apart,

13
00:00:51,347 --> 00:00:54,110
and brother turned against brother.

14
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:58,680
At a festival in Prabhas Tirth,
the quarrel grew so wild,

15
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:02,151
that the whole Yadava
clan destroyed itself.

16
00:01:02,271 --> 00:01:07,080
Heartbroken, Shri Krishna sat down
to rest under a tree in the forest.

17
00:01:07,876 --> 00:01:13,170
Just then, a hunter named Jara shot
an arrow, and it struck his foot.

18
00:01:13,290 --> 00:01:15,095
Jara had thought it was a deer.

19
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:22,312
Shri Krishna forgave Jara, and
returned to his divine home.

20
00:01:22,432 --> 00:01:25,984
That place is now Bhalka
Tirth, near Somnath.

21
00:01:26,908 --> 00:01:30,936
And the moment he left,
the sea rose over Dwarka.

22
00:01:31,231 --> 00:01:35,803
The waves surged, and in no time,
the whole city went under water.

23
00:01:37,311 --> 00:01:40,526
Now the question is,
is this just a story,

24
00:01:40,546 --> 00:01:43,627
or is there some truth hidden behind it?

25
00:01:43,751 --> 00:01:47,239
To find the answer, scientists
went down into the sea.

26
00:01:48,213 --> 00:01:50,457
Between two thousand five and seven,

27
00:01:50,477 --> 00:01:54,754
archaeologists and Navy divers went
digging in the waters of Dwarka.

28
00:01:57,557 --> 00:02:02,035
Below, they found stone anchors,
statues and circular structures.

29
00:02:02,559 --> 00:02:05,114
But how old are they? Right here,

30
00:02:05,134 --> 00:02:08,100
scientists are still fiercely divided.

31
00:02:09,472 --> 00:02:12,684
Now the latest news.
In twenty twenty five,

32
00:02:12,704 --> 00:02:19,995
a new underwater team from the Archaeological
Survey began exploring Dwarka and Bet Dwarka again.

33
00:02:20,199 --> 00:02:21,911
And in twenty twenty four,

34
00:02:21,931 --> 00:02:25,110
Prime Minister Modi himself
dived into this sea,

35
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:26,929
and prayed under the water.

36
00:02:27,404 --> 00:02:30,818
First, the Dwarkadhish
Temple. It has five floors,

37
00:02:30,838 --> 00:02:33,173
and stands on seventy two pillars.

38
00:02:34,807 --> 00:02:39,092
At the top, a fifty two yard flag
flutters proudly in the wind.

39
00:02:39,429 --> 00:02:42,866
Then the Gomti Ghat, where
the river Gomti hugs the sea.

40
00:02:45,092 --> 00:02:46,942
Do visit the Rukmini Temple too,

41
00:02:46,962 --> 00:02:49,474
the temple of Shri
Krishna's queen Rukmini.

42
00:02:50,754 --> 00:02:53,847
And Bet Dwarka, an island
in the middle of the sea,

43
00:02:53,867 --> 00:02:57,347
which you can now reach straight
over the Sudarshan Setu.

44
00:02:58,657 --> 00:03:00,737
So remember these four places,

45
00:03:01,658 --> 00:03:02,869
Dwarkadhish Temple,

46
00:03:03,638 --> 00:03:04,706
Gomti Ghat,

47
00:03:05,299 --> 00:03:06,481
Rukmini Temple,

48
00:03:06,819 --> 00:03:07,868
and Bet Dwarka.

49
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,633
Now the question, how do you get there?

50
00:03:13,182 --> 00:03:16,876
Dwarka railway station is just
two kilometres from the temple.

51
00:03:17,552 --> 00:03:21,749
Vehicles cannot reach the
temple, so walk the last stretch.

52
00:03:22,697 --> 00:03:25,942
Darshan here has no charge,
it is completely free.

53
00:03:26,461 --> 00:03:29,752
Darshan timings are six
thirty to one in the morning,

54
00:03:29,772 --> 00:03:32,209
and five to nine thirty in the evening.

55
00:03:32,566 --> 00:03:36,681
Timings change on festivals,
so check the official website.

56
00:03:37,110 --> 00:03:41,248
Bet Dwarka is about thirty
two kilometres away,

57
00:03:41,268 --> 00:03:44,365
and the Sudarshan Setu has no toll.

58
00:03:44,485 --> 00:03:47,413
The best season to visit
is October to March.

59
00:03:48,815 --> 00:03:50,092
Now let us plan one day.

60
00:03:51,316 --> 00:03:52,811
At six thirty in the morning,

61
00:03:52,831 --> 00:03:55,442
have your first darshan
at the Dwarkadhish Temple.

62
00:03:56,819 --> 00:03:59,285
At eight, stroll along the Gomti Ghat.

63
00:04:00,417 --> 00:04:05,376
In the afternoon, cross the Sudarshan
Setu and explore Bet Dwarka.

64
00:04:05,906 --> 00:04:10,592
And in the evening, enjoy the evening
aarti at the Dwarkadhish Temple.

65
00:04:12,277 --> 00:04:16,372
Remember, you cannot take phones
and bags inside the temple,

66
00:04:16,392 --> 00:04:17,901
keep them in a locker.

67
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:21,254
Keep your clothes simple and modest.

68
00:04:21,501 --> 00:04:24,140
Carry a water bottle,
wear comfortable shoes,

69
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:26,524
and keep a little patience in the crowd.

70
00:04:28,624 --> 00:04:32,755
The truth is, Dwarka is not just a
city, it is an unfinished question.

71
00:04:35,147 --> 00:04:39,692
Dwarka sank into the sea, but
our channel must not sink, bro.

72
00:04:41,311 --> 00:04:43,756
So subscribe, and save it from drowning.
